# UI, Layout & Localisation

## Responsive

- Use `AppLayoutBloc` → `AppVersionEnum` (`mobile` | `tablet` | `desk`).
- Breakpoints: desk width `> 1024`, tablet shortestSide `>= 600` (`GameConstants`).
- **No** `flutter_screenutil` or global scaling packages.
- Every new surface must work on phone **and** tablet/desktop/macOS.

```dart
BlocSelector<AppLayoutBloc, AppLayoutState, AppVersionEnum>(
  selector: (s) => s.appVersion,
  builder: (context, appVersion) { /* Row vs Column, padding */ },
)
```

## Shared chrome

Prefer `lib/core/widgets/`: `SectionCard`, `AppBorderContainer`, `AppDivider`, `AppScrollbar`, `InfoRow`, `ActionButton`, `AmountTextField`, `AppDialog`, `ProgressBarWidget`.

## Localisation

- **No hardcoded user-facing strings** — `context.l10n` / `AppLocalizations`.
- Add keys to `lib/l10n/app_en.arb`, then `flutter gen-l10n`.

## Scaffolding

- Prefer existing screen shell (`CellsScreen` + tab content) over ad-hoc raw layouts.
- When introducing a new full screen later, keep one consistent scaffold wrapper; do not mix random `Scaffold` styles.
